                  "type": "END"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Input Extractor"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1773706041443"
                  },
                  "code": "INPUT_EXTRACTOR",
                  "id": "1773363458200",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773363458201_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "Extract the user input from the following: {{$context.$nodes.BULK_PROCESSOR.$currentItem}} \nIf the supply document header number (that usually appears after the supply type) related data is present extract it into `SupplySourceHeaderNumber` output. Note: For On Hand Supply there won't be any supply document header number leave it empty. \nIf the supply document line number related data is present extract it into the `SupplySourceLineNumber` output. Note: For On Hand Supply there won't be any supply line number leave it empty.\nIf  the supply document related data is present then extract the `SupplySourceType` and `SupplySourceTypeId` refer below. If no supply source type is mentioned set `SupplySourceTypeId` as an empty string \"\".\n| DOCUMENT TYPE | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE         | SUPPLY SOURCE TYPE ID |  \n            | ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------- |  \n            | Supply        | On hand                    | 13                    |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order             | 1                     |  \n            | Supply        | Purchase order requisition | 17                    |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order             | 8                     |  \n            | Supply        | Transfer order return      | 18                    |  \n            | Supply        | Work order                 | 5                     |\nIf the demand document related data is present then extract the `DemandSourceTypeId` and `DemandSourceType` from the below table. \n  | DOCUMENT TYPE | DEMAND SOURCE TYPE    | DEMAND SOURCE TYPE ID |  \n            | ------------- | --------------------- | --------------------- |  \n            | Demand        | Sales order           | 2                     |  \n            | Demand        | Transfer order        | 8                     |  \n            | Demand        | Transfer order return | 18                    |  \n            | Demand        | Work order            | 5                     |  \n            | Demand        | Purchase order        | 1                     |  \n            | Demand        | Account               | 3                     |  \n            | Demand        | Account alias         | 6                     |  \n            | Demand        | Cycle count           | 9                     |  \n            | Demand        | User defined          | 13                    |\nUse natural language procesing to identify the values for the each attribute of the following list:\n\nReservationRequirementDate\nReservationQuantity\nDemandSourceTypeId\nDemandSourceHeaderNumber\nDemandSourceLineNumber (this will be followed by DemandSourceHeaderNumber, this is also referred to as line in the context of demand)\nReservationUnitOfMeasure\nOperationSequenceNumber (this is only applicable if DemandSourceTypeId is 5)\nItemNumber\nSupplySourceTypeId\nSupplySourceHeaderNumber, a supply is mentioned in the form “against supply {SupplySourceType} {token}”, treat {token} as SupplySourceHeaderNumber even if it contains letters/hyphens (e.g., SDFSD-SDF43SD). \nSupplySourceLineNumber, we find this alongside SupplySourceHeaderNumber. This string is an identifier of a specific line within the supply document."
                    }
                  ],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"OperationSequenceNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"DemandSourceTypeId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"SupplySourceLineNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"SupplySourceHeaderNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"DemandSourceHeaderNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ReservationRequirementDate\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ReservationQuantity\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"DemandSourceLineNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ReservationUnitOfMeasure\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ItemNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"SupplySourceTypeId\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
